        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Holomorphic functions are the central object of complex analysis. The Cauchy-Riemann equations are the bridge from the algebraic definition (limit of difference quotient exists) to the analytic structure (power series, harmonic parts). Understanding *why* CR equations are both necessary and sufficient (with continuity) is the entry point for everything else."
